#===============================================================================
# QUIET-LAYER TEST — Sharket 3.29 Ruthless
#
# The previous version of this file FAILED TO LOAD. Cause found: an agent wrote
# `SetTextColor 0 0 0 0`, and the game rejects an alpha channel on TEXT.
# Nothing in any shipped filter uses it — not FilterBlade, not our V7.0, not
# Sharket 3.27. Only Sharket 3.15 did, and that predates the Show/Hide option.
#
# ★ THE RECIPE BELOW IS NOT INVENTED. It is copied verbatim from the author's
#   own `Sharket3.27[0]无情异界私货.ruthlessfilter`, which uses it 5 times under
#   the comment `全局设置 - 显示全部垃圾物品` ("global setting — show all trash"):
#
#       Show
#           <conditions>
#           SetBackgroundColor 0 0 0 0
#           SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
#           SetFontSize 1
#           DisableDropSound
#
#   No SetTextColor. Alpha 0 on BACKGROUND and BORDER only — both of which are
#   shipped today by FilterBlade 3.29 and by our own V7.0. And `SetFontSize 1`
#   is proven legal, because that filter loaded and shipped.
#
# SO THIS IS A CONFIRMATION, NOT AN EXPLORATION. Two questions remain:
#   Q1  Does the 3.27 recipe still work in 3.29?          -> C vs the canary
#   Q2  Is it actually quieter than what we ship now?     -> C vs B
#       B is a bare `Minimal`, exactly what V7.0 emits for a hidden item.
#       If C is invisible and B is not, we should stop emitting Minimal for the
#       quiet layer and emit an invisible Show instead.
#
# HOW TO RUN
#   1. Select this filter.
#   2. Hideout. Drop the three items below in a row, in order A, B, C.
#   3. Read the labels. Your item highlight is always on, so no Alt needed.
#   4. Note whether C has a label at all, and whether it is still clickable.
#
# ⚠️ If this STILL refuses to load, the remaining suspect is `SetFontSize 1`.
#    Comment out that one line in block C (add a leading #) and reload. If it
#    then loads, 3.29 tightened the font-size range since 3.27 — report that,
#    it is the answer and it kills the idea.
#===============================================================================


#--- CANARY — must render HUGE and RED. If you cannot see this, the filter did
#    not load, and nothing else on this page means anything.
Show
    BaseType == "Scroll of Wisdom"
    SetFontSize 45
    SetTextColor 255 255 255 255
    SetBackgroundColor 200 0 0 255
    SetBorderColor 255 255 255 255


#--- B · BARE MINIMAL — exactly what V7.0 emits for every hidden item.
#    This is the thing we are trying to beat.
Minimal
    BaseType == "Portal Scroll"


#--- C · THE SHARKET 3.27 RECIPE, copied verbatim. A Show block, no SetTextColor.
Show
    BaseType == "Armourer's Scrap"
    SetBackgroundColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    SetFontSize 1
    DisableDropSound


#--- D · the same recipe as a MINIMAL block rather than a Show.
#    If C is invisible and D is not, Minimal ignores style and the quiet layer
#    has to be built from Shows. If both are invisible, either will do and
#    Minimal is preferable — it keeps the "this is hidden" meaning in the file.
Minimal
    BaseType == "Blacksmith's Whetstone"
    SetBackgroundColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    SetFontSize 1
    DisableDropSound


#--- everything else keeps a normal label so the game stays playable
Show
